{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he left his garment with her.</b> Scripture teaches his merit, that he did not wish to struggle with his mistress to take his garment from her, but left it with her out of respect for her." "<b>And he fled and went outside.</b> He went outside so that she would despair of him and not pursue him further. Or perhaps, because the righteous man wished to conquer his impulse, he contrived to find a way and went outside to cool off, for the forces of his body had grown hot." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״And he fled and went outside.״ The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: You fled today — the sea shall flee before your ark, as is said (Psalms 114:3): ״הים ראה וינוס״ — 'The sea saw and fled.' What did it see? The ark of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:54.092445069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}